{"shortDescription":"By Avinash  P and Ragini MathurLatin American currencies weakened on Monday as the U.S. dollar rose, while escalating conflict in the Middle East drove oil prices higher and pushed Treasury yields to fresh highs, souring risk appetite.Global investors started the week on a shaky note as oil extende…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["By Avinash  P and Ragini Mathur"]},{"type":"p","children":["Latin American currencies weakened on Monday as the U.S. dollar rose, while escalating conflict in the Middle East drove oil prices higher and pushed Treasury yields to fresh highs, souring risk appetite."]},{"type":"p","children":["Global investors started the week on a shaky note as oil extended its rally after fresh strikes on Saudi Arabian energy infrastructure and attacks on ships in the Middle East compounded supply concerns."]},{"type":"p","children":["Benchmark 10-year U.S. Treasury yields climbed to the key 5% level for the first time since October 2023, adding pressure on developing-market assets."]},{"type":"p","children":["Higher U.S. yields make dollar-denominated investments more attractive, potentially drawing capital away from emerging economies."]},{"type":"p","children":["The U.S. Federal Reserve is widely expected to raise its main lending rate by at least 25 basis points this week, a sharp shift from just a week ago, when markets saw roughly even odds of a hike or a pause."]},{"type":"p","children":["An index tracking Latin American currencies (.MILA00000CUS) fell 0.9%, while the U.S. dollar ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"TVC:DXY","text":"TVC:DXY"}}," strengthened 0.4%."]},{"type":"p","children":["Warnings from leaders of major AI companies about the technology's potential risks also weighed on broader risk sentiment, lending further support to the dollar."]},{"type":"p","children":["Most Latin American equity indexes also declined as metal prices, a key source of export revenue for the region, came under pressure. MSCI's regional stocks index (.MILA00000PUS) dropped 1.2%."]},{"type":"p","children":["BRAZIL ASSETS EYED AS ELECTIONS, RATE DECISION LOOM"]},{"type":"p","children":["Two polls released on Monday showed Brazilian President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva and right-wing Senator Flavio Bolsonaro statistically tied in a potential second-round runoff ahead of next month's election."]},{"type":"p","children":["Brazilian markets had rallied in recent sessions as polls showed Flavio Bolsonaro narrowing the gap. Investors generally view him as more market-friendly, so signs that Lula is recovering ground weighed on local assets."]},{"type":"p","children":["Separately, Brazil's central bank is expected to cut interest rates by a quarter point for a fifth straight meeting on Wednesday, according to a Reuters poll of economists."]},{"type":"p","children":["\"Since the last Copom meeting, the news flow has been mixed for the inflation outlook. The global environment has deteriorated, while domestic indicators continue to point to economic deceleration and disinflation,\" XP analysts said in a note."]},{"type":"p","children":["\"This combination should reinforce the Copom's cautious stance, though it will not prevent another rate cut.\""]},{"type":"p","children":["At 14.00%, the Selic benchmark rate is one of the highest in the world among major economies. Data on Friday showed the country's annual inflation cooled, paving the way for further rate easing."]},{"type":"p","children":["Elsewhere, Chile's peso ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"FX_IDC:USDCLP","text":"FX_IDC:USDCLP"}}," weakened 1% to its lowest level in nearly 11 months as copper prices slid to multweek lows . Chile is the world's top copper exporter. Local stocks (.MICL00000PUS) eased 0.7%."]},{"type":"p","children":["Mexico's peso ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"FX_IDC:USDMXN","text":"FX_IDC:USDMXN"}}," fell 1% to its weakest level in a month, though local stocks ",{"type":"symbol","param